  "scientific_conclusion": "Prospective four-channel ECELLE_V3_2 optical SETI survey across 159 exposures of 22 fresh FGKM stars (90 HARPS + 69 VLT ESPRESSO; 34 control exposures on 4 non-planet stars + 125 science exposures across 18 confirmed exoplanet hosts with 41 planets at 1.30-114.3 pc, including 5 full transit-night timeseries and 12 solar-neighborhood <10 pc exoplanet systems) completed: Keplerian planetary-rest-frame de-Doppler stacking (Channel K_PLANET) increased moving-planet CW laser recovery at >=6.5 sigma/exp from 0.0% (uncompensated T_DIFF) to 67.3%, while reducing Legacy V2's 1552 false alarms (1446 science) to 0 control and 21 science V3.2 survivors across all 4 channels (T, P, T_DIFF, K_PLANET), setting 8-sigma 10 m beamed laser upper limits down to 9.0 W (0.0090 kW) on Proxima Centauri (PROXIMACEN, d = 1.302 pc) and completing a unified 60-star (349-exposure) D079+D080+D081 optical SETI synthesis covering 18 stars within 10 pc."
